{%- assign tool_key = include.tool_key -%}
{%- assign tool_meta = page.tools[tool_key] -%}
{%- assign tool_name = include.tool | default: tool_meta.name | default: page.tool | default: "tool" -%}
{%- assign exec_name = include.exec | default: tool_meta.exec | default: tool_name -%}
{%- assign software_root = include.root | default: "/software/el9/apps" -%}
{%- assign tool_path = include.path | default: software_root -%}
{%- assign tool_version = include.version | default: '' -%}
{%- assign requirements = include.required | default: '' -%}

<div class="margin-y-2" markdown="1">

The `{{ tool_name }}` is available under `{{ software_root }}`. The executable `{{ exec_name }}` may be nested under a tool and version directory.

Confirm the executable path:
```bash
find "{{ tool_path }}" -type f -name "{{ exec_name }}" -print
```

Set the `TOOL_PATH` shell variable for selected tool version and add it to your `PATH`:
```bash
TOOL_PATH="{{ tool_path }}{% if tool_version %}/{{ tool_version }}{% endif %}"
export PATH="${TOOL_PATH}:$PATH"
```
{% if include.required != '' %}
{{ requirements }}
{% endif %}

</div>
